{"name":"Arnica","hex":"#bf8f37","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Arnica","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A taxonomic genus within the family Asteraceae – arnica plants."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Arnica"}],"entries":[{"title":"Arnica","blocks":[{"text":"Arnica is a genus of perennial, herbaceous plants in the sunflower family (Asteraceae). The genus name Arnica may be derived from the Greek arni, \"lamb\", in reference to the plants' soft, hairy leaves. Arnica is also known by the names mountain tobacco and, confusingly, leopard's bane and wolfsbane—two names that it shares with the entirely unrelated genus Aconitum."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/17/Arnica_montana_-_K%C3%B6hler%E2%80%93s_Medizinal-Pflanzen-015.jpg/330px-Arnica_montana_-_K%C3%B6hler%E2%80%93s_Medizinal-Pflanzen-015.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Arnica","wikidata":"Q693908"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7f/Arnica_chamissonis0.jpg/250px-Arnica_chamissonis0.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7f/Arnica_chamissonis0.jpg/500px-Arnica_chamissonis0.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7f/Arnica_chamissonis0.jpg/250px-Arnica_chamissonis0.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AArnica_chamissonis0.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b7/Arnica_griscomii.jpg/250px-Arnica_griscomii.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b7/Arnica_griscomii.jpg/500px-Arnica_griscomii.jpg?utm_sou